    {
        "content": "<p>Hi <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1025178\">@Pranav Magdum</span>. Nice. </p>\n<p>I'm not sure if it is because a copy-and-paste but the formatting of this code block seems odd (i.e. no indents). </p>\n<p>This in general looks very good! There are a couple of things I would change to make it better though: </p>\n<ol>\n<li>I would only put the physical input data into <code>FreeParticle</code> - i.e. mass and the statement that it is positive (also convention says it should start with a capital because it is a type).  </li>\n<li>I would then define the kinetic energy, and the velocity as functions of <code>FreeParticle</code> and a given trajectory (map from <code>Time</code> to <code>ℝ</code> or <code>Space</code>) </li>\n<li>I would then expect <code>evol</code> to be a proposition on trajectories (maybe of the form that the trajectory satifies Newton's second law, or conservation of energy).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>These are naturally design choices, but I think better reflect the underlying physics, and make it more amenable for generalization.</p>",
        "id": 592741510,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1777901234
    },
