    },
    {
        "content": "<p>made my first PR :)</p>",
        "id": 593025768,
        "sender_full_name": "Pranav Magdum",
        "timestamp": 1777991889
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was trying to prove the sorryful result, </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">velocity_const_of_zero_acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Time</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcont</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContDiff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v₀</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this is a standard analysis result (related to `is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero`)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_const_of_deriv_eq_zero</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but I am running into this error,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>failed to synthesize\n  NormedSpace Time ℝ\n\nHint: Additional diagnostic information may be available using the `set_option diagnostics true` command.\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>help?</p>",
        "id": 595338473,
        "sender_full_name": "Pranav Magdum",
        "timestamp": 1778860441
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think you are going to need the corresponding proof for <code>fderiv</code> not <code>deriv</code>. (In this equation the <code>deriv</code> is <code>Time.deriv</code> not <code>_root_.deriv</code>.)</p>",
        "id": 595343367,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1778861556
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero#doc\">docs#is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero</a></p>",
        "id": 595343869,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1778861685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>runs into the same issue</p>",
        "id": 595345487,
        "sender_full_name": "Pranav Magdum",
        "timestamp": 1778862155
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Weird, I don't know why <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero#doc\">docs#is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero</a> needs this condition. Maybe one option is to write <code>q</code> as <code>(q ∘ Time.toRealCLE.symm) ∘ Time.toRealCLE</code> and then use the chain rule. to get derivatives of <code>(q ∘ Time.toRealCLE.symm) </code> and <code>Time.toRealCLE</code>. Should be able to show that the derivative of <code>(q ∘ Time.toRealCLE.symm) </code> is constant from assumptions.</p>",
        "id": 595350653,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1778863589
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>actually this issue pops up</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>failed to synthesize\nNormedSpace ?𝕜 Time\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 595351732,
        "sender_full_name": "Pranav Magdum",
        "timestamp": 1778863938
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1025178\">Pranav Magdum</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/479953-Physlib/topic/Free.20particle/near/595351732\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>actually this issue pops up</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>failed to synthesize\nNormedSpace ?𝕜 Time\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can you try enabling the detailed diagnostics once as hinted in the error prompt and then use llm to spot anything you may have missed? I have relied on this trick at times ...</p>",
        "id": 595352057,
        "sender_full_name": "Shlok Vaibhav",
        "timestamp": 1778864033
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"917541\">@Shlok Vaibhav</span> <br>\nThis is what chat-gpt says</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>We’ve hit a Lean typeclass issue with Time.\n\nEven though Time is just a wrapper over ℝ, Lean treats it as a new type and doesn’t automatically inherit real analysis structure.\n\nBecause of this, calculus tools like fderiv fail with errors like:\n\nNormedSpace ?𝕜 Time\n\nLean can’t infer that Time should behave like a normed vector space over ℝ, even though mathematically it is.\n\nSo the core issue is:\n\nWe defined Time ≃ ℝ, but didn’t explicitly transfer the vector space / normed space structure, so mathlib doesn’t treat Time as ℝ for analysis.\n\nFix options:\n\nexplicitly transfer structures via the equivalence Time ≃ ℝ, or\nsimplest: define Time := ℝ (abbrev) to avoid all inference issues.\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 595361044,
        "sender_full_name": "Pranav Magdum",
        "timestamp": 1778866692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1025178\">Pranav Magdum</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/479953-Physlib/topic/Free.20particle/near/595351732\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>actually this issue pops up</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>failed to synthesize\nNormedSpace ?𝕜 Time\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Lean is saying it doesn't know what <code>𝕜</code> is, you can tell it by <code>(𝕜 := ℝ)</code></p>\n<p>i.e. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 595390046,
        "sender_full_name": "ZhiKai Pong",
        "timestamp": 1778876133
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>general question: why not make velocity and accel <code>abbrev</code>s?</p>",
        "id": 595390940,
        "sender_full_name": "ZhiKai Pong",
        "timestamp": 1778876508
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A few comments about this file which you might want to consider, or we could go through in your next PR:</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>comments</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<ol>\n<li>I would replace all <code>deriv</code> with <code>∂ₜ</code>, otherwise it's confusing which <code>deriv</code> you are talking about</li>\n<li>I think your current <code>velocity_const_of_zero_acct</code> should really be API in Time.Derivatives, and then this file just references it. </li>\n<li>generally, I think <code>obtain</code> is preferred over <code>rcases</code>, i.e. in your final proof you can do <code>obtain ⟨v₀, hv⟩ := velocity_const_of_zero_acc q h_acc hcont</code> (or if you fancy, inlining <code>hcc</code> as well, i.e. <code>obtain ⟨v₀, hv⟩ := velocity_const_of_zero_acc q (accel_zero s q h) hcont</code></li>\n<li>ideally we want to avoid <code>unfold</code> as much as possible, in this case you could just <code>rw [kineticEnergy, velocity]</code> here</li>\n</ol>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 595397192,
        "sender_full_name": "ZhiKai Pong",
        "timestamp": 1778878817
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Got it to work</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">velocity_const_of_zero_acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Time</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcont</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v₀</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this is a standard analysis result (related to `is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero`)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_const_of_fderiv_eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcont</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>does this look good, should I make a PR?</p>",
        "id": 595489113,
